 field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c47e99b0-49b1-5362-97e1-164913960980" :question/math-academy-id "q-119774" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=8{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=8{x}^{2}{y}^{2}.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/d1/d1e4f48450a7f2032d755a5255d1a1e8a726dd16d273dae5dc1e587826d5ce58.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253604 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172041 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75710e99-e13c-54ba-9401-486bfec15284" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rectangular Regions Where a Slope Field Is Positive or Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63bf1a57-3783-5d79-86d4-63b09128f121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437576} {:answer/id #uuid "b93e4ca2-69b6-5a23-92dc-bd3e12591fac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b93e4ca2-69b6-5a23-92dc-bd3e12591fac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437577} :answer-field/id #uuid "0546cbf1-39ac-5e9a-b792-688818e61d96" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438817} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b5e7f32-fc04-5ce5-b770-d86f4a5801bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437578} {:answer/id #uuid "d4629f24-fcf3-5347-a5a8-7f5e988f4f6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4629f24-fcf3-5347-a5a8-7f5e988f4f6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437579} :answer-field/id #uuid "7824ba84-f876-58c2-b30b-6da65a0f46fb" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438818} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bc54d78-4834-5ecc-a21c-1bace28776a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437580} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd678d7-15ac-548b-b810-649d7913e7db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cd678d7-15ac-548b-b810-649d7913e7db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437581} :answer-field/id #uuid "de2afb91-baf3-53b2-8e4a-7316ea92bfe0" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "635d0331-704b-5958-9f79-2f8d94fa4111" :question/math-academy-id "q-119797" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(2-x)(y+1)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=(2-x)(y+1).$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=2$ or $y=-1.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/ca/caa61190f1a5565c58838556529715c08f9f00402c6f4b3ccb99a914e748f198.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/01/01e91ecf01cfc64ed87e29081a6b9f8a3fc5afade1b25be08039b8778d981cf7.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive” is true. If $x>2$ and $y<-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative” is true. If $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive” is true. If $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive”; “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative”; “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253605 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172041 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75710e99-e13c-54ba-9401-486bfec15284" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rectangular Regions Where a Slope Field Is Positive or Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e1be2fa-de0d-5f22-b440-911091c56105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437582} {:answer/id #uuid "75d08e9a-c55b-5a67-abb2-4e27159b9b63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e1be2fa-de0d-5f22-b440-911091c56105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437582} :answer-field/id #uuid "8390e0db-2166-50f2-a123-b7b9177c8341" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y>2,$ the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438820} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3164774-f189-596d-acdb-746f708a14aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437584} {:answer/id #uuid "e364779c-88b2-5f8d-ac35-11f4c01ba4f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3164774-f189-596d-acdb-746f708a14aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437584} :answer-field/id #uuid "a904fb7a-832f-5a30-ac49-1d6d8c3a62e6" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>1$ and $y<2,$ the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438821} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b51910a4-e37d-5c34-adb4-b2218d1f40f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437586} {:answer/id #uuid "5ab61bfa-dc48-58d5-a149-9bf36c574b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b51910a4-e37d-5c34-adb4-b2218d1f40f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437586} :answer-field/id #uuid "71947ae8-7e46-57cd-b733-f67a0fa6d76c" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y<2,$ the slope of the slope field is positive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dff46479-0340-5239-b8ff-db620f2c9a7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-119800" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(1-x)(y-2)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=(1-x)(y-2).$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=1$ or $y=2.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/47/47784a3201e93648e495827b12078073cc9f1a03cd3c11904a875bad10a3bde2.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/73/73631c178777b4489e35fa87d08474ccf2b8b484b9bf5fe7272b1ce25d45f1b0.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y>2,$ the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $x<1$ and $y>2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>1$ and $y<2,$ the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $x>1$ and $y<2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y<2,$ the slope of the slope field is positive” is false. If $x<1$ and $y<2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253607 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172041 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75710e99-e13c-54ba-9401-486bfec15284" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rectangular Regions Where a Slope Field Is Positive or Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9e11f01-32e2-5138-b450-b28abfcfe393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437588} {:answer/id #uuid "eba29a8a-cdc7-5437-a377-49e424a33c92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9e11f01-32e2-5138-b450-b28abfcfe393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437588} :answer-field/id #uuid "6731a097-fbbb-5d0d-924d-44214b41bafb" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438823} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67be040e-e5a2-539e-bae4-03679cb8d0dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437590} {:answer/id #uuid "989c32ec-026e-53bf-8bf8-04e72bb618bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "989c32ec-026e-53bf-8bf8-04e72bb618bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437591} :answer-field/id #uuid "27e31d3a-247b-506c-a5ca-66c30896d048" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438824} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ffef47e-2f1a-52ce-9ce8-8cc5126973d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437592} {:answer/id #uuid "82c17871-30b3-570d-9985-cbfb4030107c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82c17871-30b3-570d-9985-cbfb4030107c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437593} :answer-field/id #uuid "300b0a1c-8c14-56f6-b340-cad908fc709b" :answer-field/key "At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2a6ca6d7-d1ef-5811-9457-4d7cf9a54890" :question/math-academy-id "q-119816" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(x-2)^{2}(y+1)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=(x-2)^{2}(y+1).$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=2$ or $y=-1.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/ca/caa61190f1a5565c58838556529715c08f9f00402c6f4b3ccb99a914e748f198.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/d8/d836463631120853e05b3b5fb9e534822cf5611747a3eb17e22333901bfb8fd3.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative” is true. If $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive” is true. If $x>2$ and $y>-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative”; “At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253631 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ede6800b-ecfd-5ef8-a386-4aec94ddd89c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Stationary Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ff08fd4-e76a-5634-bb6e-0c9a6b0b3993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461887} {:answer/id #uuid "5cdb674f-ffd4-54b9-8c1e-4f91a2dc3f5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ff08fd4-e76a-5634-bb6e-0c9a6b0b3993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461887} :answer-field/id #uuid "82e63362-cab2-5e7e-83e8-f22d22398220" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=x-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e608e253-42d4-5961-8843-52ddbcf614d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461889} {:answer/id #uuid "9ff0fdb5-8f4c-57c8-a23f-45439729d652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ff0fdb5-8f4c-57c8-a23f-45439729d652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461890} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0864e24-ac68-556b-ac40-cfab9960b432" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}={x}^{2}(x-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462698} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbff8f6c-be50-5006-8ae5-e8ea53b23903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461891} {:answer/id #uuid "6120c7e4-6551-59ac-890c-ed12d399ae95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbff8f6c-be50-5006-8ae5-e8ea53b23903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461891} :answer-field/id #uuid "90e05925-1a87-58ef-9da7-8a4d05b06a6d" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=x(x+1)(x-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462699}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf3614e8-6b2e-5b66-a1c3-8c10682d44be" :question/math-academy-id "q-120025" :question/problem "![](images/17/17cd72acbe8dd412d37c51ff992278d9664f6c5b1141a8604278fda76e57700f.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/5d/5d6165488c8e41c16cf31b1b000a924344399c2b94a8fe5e7138c55adf97602b.png)\n\nNotice that the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=0$ and $x=2,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each equation:\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=x-2$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side does not evaluate to zero at both $x=0$ and $x=2.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}(x-2)$ gives the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $x=2.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=x(x+1)(x-2)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $x=2,$ but it also evaluates to zero when $x=-1,$ which is not a behavior exhibited by our slope field.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}(x-2)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166821 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5277f56d-3f2d-505c-bf73-48207a2310a3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using the Sign of the Slopes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "982cc208-4ef7-53b6-b14e-eddf19d4f7f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461893} {:answer/id #uuid "dc4796b3-871f-5f81-a235-937da5930fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc4796b3-871f-5f81-a235-937da5930fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461894} :answer-field/id #uuid "313eb125-e9e4-5cbd-b384-ea16df717365" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{10}(x+3)(x-2)^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc9b1942-b0bc-54f8-a6c3-1ff051b6a113" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461895} {:answer/id #uuid "e858c129-3cbe-507d-9eca-9bb753521056" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc9b1942-b0bc-54f8-a6c3-1ff051b6a113" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461895} :answer-field/id #uuid "da434888-6e69-5683-b144-41c6022c0ca0" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{5}(x+3)(2-x)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462701} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2191303c-5047-5ef5-8284-5beaca1777ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461897} {:answer/id #uuid "6eab0a1c-68e9-523d-9519-74a67c6d7470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2191303c-5047-5ef5-8284-5beaca1777ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461897} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf290901-b724-5bf9-b2cb-39afaae04ac0" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=(x+2)(x-3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a07799d5-cf00-5be4-9950-028a4e658d3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-120038" :question/problem "![](images/f8/f855062048a7d38b2fa6c843701a182661b2235b2042ad83fbedd600b1dd770c.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "![](images/8f/8fdec9bda9e2bcc514e56a14a6608b2f0cb74fd0943a51c944b29cc047e02cd9.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=-3$ and $x=2.$ Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\n- Second, the lines $x=-3$ and $x=2$ divide the plane into $3$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $3$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| Region | $x<-3$ | $-3<x<2$ | $x>2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↘$ | $↗$ | $↗$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{10}(x+3)(x-2)^{2}$ gives the required behavior.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{5}(x+3)(2-x)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-3$ and $x=2,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| Region | $x<-3$ | $-3<x<2$ | $x>2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↘$ | $↗$ | $↘$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=(x+2)(x-3)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-2$ and $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{10}(x+3)(x-2)^{2}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253637 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166860 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "762c5225-00bd-5d2f-9859-394f886482cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using the Sign of the Slopes and Factoring"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "278ae8de-7b07-5a39-bd04-2bf57e898f0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461899} {:answer/id #uuid "b8e575c9-1a51-597f-84b4-2c9662352a5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8e575c9-1a51-597f-84b4-2c9662352a5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461900} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a25f6e5-8bae-5e17-a73e-a1406b38edcd" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}={x}^{2}+3x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462703} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16036a91-f98e-56f8-b955-49aab5c89324" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461901} {:answer/id #uuid "66df9c9a-852d-5e75-85f8-abb65b295796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16036a91-f98e-56f8-b955-49aab5c89324" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461901} :answer-field/id #uuid "e21ab9c9-0c3d-5925-b233-b032c143454e" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}={x}^{2}+x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462704} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d7a83a5-f0b5-5e63-82b6-ca77f186d3d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461903} {:answer/id #uuid "d9f8f614-5859-5fce-bd83-5ac2a8102396" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d7a83a5-f0b5-5e63-82b6-ca77f186d3d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461903} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab2eae38-ac46-5aa4-97fa-3b62105e8528" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}={x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462705}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b69e6ff7-5b7e-5a36-bad5-97913bd7c4d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-120070" :question/problem "![](images/51/51273365c4a282dc3dedd9d7cd5ac7d805e1526aaeee1915e8bd95d8223c26d3.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/a1/a14651ffc883a8c24ad17bdd031658c3d4ae21db2cfded213f2ba911fdb9a765.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slope field is zero along the lines $x=-3$ and $x=0.$ Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\n- Second, the lines $x=-3$ and $x=0$ divide the plane into $3$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $3$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| Region | $x<-3$ | $-3<x<0$ | $x>0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↗$ | $↘$ | $↗$ |\n| Sign | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}+3x=x(x+3)\n$$\n\ngives the required behavior.\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}+x=x(x+1)\n$$\n\ndoes *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-1$ and $x=0.$\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}={x}^{2}(x+3)\n$$\n\ndoes *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $x=-3$ and $x=0,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| Region | $x<-3$ | $-3<x<0$ | $x>0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↘$ | $↗$ | $↗$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}+3x$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253640 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166822 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32b9a92b-880b-50de-b8e9-648fa219b83f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Asymptotes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57428bd5-b536-5679-aea6-fd81151b1b05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461905} {:answer/id #uuid "eca1e859-1f88-5247-ad2a-b6421e23665a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57428bd5-b536-5679-aea6-fd81151b1b05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461905} :answer-field/id #uuid "32e6e343-0561-57a5-bca5-94897a041baa" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}={x}^{2}(x+1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462706} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26e488bb-c9eb-5f1c-9403-74a0fb15149d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461907} {:answer/id #uuid "f9d9969f-476f-5ff9-80c3-e734d4ba0b1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26e488bb-c9eb-5f1c-9403-74a0fb15149d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461907} :answer-field/id #uuid "65a0c5b6-3109-51ca-821e-2d69c40f39f0" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x+1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462707} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1cdc35e-ec49-5951-a0f1-9d4314c0e098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461909} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e49dca-fa51-5326-9677-f3a2d54d14d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7e49dca-fa51-5326-9677-f3a2d54d14d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461910} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ba20859-bde5-5414-ae2b-f393052e586d" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x+1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c84723b8-0d5e-5a26-bf52-a830d4f235da" :question/math-academy-id "q-120076" :question/problem "![](images/5f/5fdb2ddd3d07537c1e3d0d22d435928f7cd11dc7a71c67f1bf45292c82a61ef7.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/cf/cf2ba44d8cc21ade2204a3784af7d09b492843339a8b98c4cde741b30dfa54db.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- The solution curves have the vertical asymptote $x=-1.$\n\n- The slopes of the slope field become vertical as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}(x+1)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side does not approach $\\pm \\infty $ as $x\\to -1.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x+1}$ does *not* give the required behavior. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{x+1}\\to 0\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for this differential equation do not approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x+1}$ gives the required behavior. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x+1}=\\frac{x}{(1+\\frac{1}{x})}\\to \\pm \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to \\pm \\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slopes of the slope field for this differential equation become vertical as $x\\to \\pm \\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x+1}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253646 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166857 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "954f8004-35b4-58ec-be26-2beccfd5f8e4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Equilibrium Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9a85761-e47d-574d-9aca-6588a7dd5c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461911} {:answer/id #uuid "25bab925-9735-5360-85d0-fde5a0511311" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9a85761-e47d-574d-9aca-6588a7dd5c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461911} :answer-field/id #uuid "edd130c4-9b30-5e75-a187-0481d77ef977" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=(y+1)(y-1)(y-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462709} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbd6c367-57f0-5f45-9efd-0993e4e7a66f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461913} {:answer/id #uuid "4f892145-d69d-5017-a426-f4fbc16458ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbd6c367-57f0-5f45-9efd-0993e4e7a66f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461913} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e1156cf-24af-5473-8988-72a4fac212ef" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=(y+1)(y-1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462710} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5eacd648-b318-52c0-a8fb-ba4fa4b7021d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461915} {:answer/id #uuid "d49308f3-03c0-5c82-91fa-efdba351adad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d49308f3-03c0-5c82-91fa-efdba351adad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461916} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2fdad47-d5a7-5a45-8713-009a1d0bf9be" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=(y+1)^{2}(2-y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462711}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c0faaaf1-6fed-5e12-af7b-9fca9c443b1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-120109" :question/problem "![](images/3d/3d24906da8cd181d40dbaec0095b8d51481babc152609fc378b03c61187220c3.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/7f/7f8a042b9944b2cdf0e864b7dca760f094f4413f197befa05d6e5cbefb3841ba.png)\n\nNotice that the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $y=-1$ and $y=2,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each equation:\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=(y+1)(y-1)(y-2)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $y=-1$ and $y=2,$ but it also evaluates to zero when $y=1,$ which is not behavior exhibited by our slope field.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=(y+1)(y-1)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $y=\\pm 1.$\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=(y+1)^{2}(2-y)$ gives the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $y=-1$ and $y=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=(y+1)^{2}(2-y)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253648 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c04b23-e341-57e9-a072-985e4b536e5a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "533214b3-6c61-52ee-85dd-a8d6006ced54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461917} {:answer/id #uuid "23c15b20-858c-5295-90c6-68f113ba9d04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "533214b3-6c61-52ee-85dd-a8d6006ced54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461917} :answer-field/id #uuid "52121635-762f-5923-b01d-1582f7ea794d" :answer-field/key "$T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462712} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7d6c812-7ee3-5e26-b033-2a4ef6caab4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461919} {:answer/id #uuid "eba0a9bc-d740-58d4-9682-e24f2ebd01d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7d6c812-7ee3-5e26-b033-2a4ef6caab4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461919} :answer-field/id #uuid "b222fe66-ffd9-5e28-8684-edf53b486030" :answer-field/key "$T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462713} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1921f4a9-2a50-5748-bfbb-ee6ebd7a5229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461921} {:answer/id #uuid "2feb6598-cea3-599a-adb9-4e0e897d27ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2feb6598-cea3-599a-adb9-4e0e897d27ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461922} :answer-field/id #uuid "79c1742e-b505-51ed-b84e-0e730cf0b35e" :answer-field/key "$T$ is **NOT** a linear transformation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462714}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a3a19c98-b506-54b2-aa6b-86aada819468" :question/math-academy-id "q-12012" :question/problem "Let \n$T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{x}^{2} \\\\ 7y\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix}=kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\  & T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}(kx)^{2} \\\\ 7(ky)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{k}^{2}({x}^{2}) \\\\ k(7y)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\begin{bmatrix}k({x}^{2}) \\\\ 7y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is not a linear transformation.\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})^{2} \\\\ 7({y}_{1}+{y}_{2})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ 7{y}_{1}+7{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}^{2} \\\\ 7{y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\ 7{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, only statement “$T$ is **NOT** a linear transformation” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253649 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166858 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ca086fd-9732-5c4b-9cb0-168433d79203" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using the Sign of the Slopes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74867da9-181e-5142-bda9-0d826272b670" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461923} {:answer/id #uuid "1b78992f-e9fe-52f1-b329-9e087aa1b71e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74867da9-181e-5142-bda9-0d826272b670" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461923} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e21d96b-7d6c-56e5-ac65-623671510a76" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}={y}^{2}(2-y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462715} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46346ac6-9690-59a2-b432-36298dc467e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461925} {:answer/id #uuid "532338a5-8803-55a0-b9a7-43ac43ec83f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "532338a5-8803-55a0-b9a7-43ac43ec83f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461926} :answer-field/id #uuid "cca5c1f4-a6cb-554d-9d1a-2a58dd0f3b9e" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=y(y-2)^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462716} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2803441-f1f5-5725-9ee8-efd9afb4532e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461927} {:answer/id #uuid "ad1e9d88-6435-5ba7-bb92-2751d20ea073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2803441-f1f5-5725-9ee8-efd9afb4532e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461927} :answer-field/id #uuid "e41132b9-d494-5928-9ebf-7b05f68c6ea3" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=y(y+2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462717}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "efa92615-fa1f-50ea-a45f-eb618f2a603d" :question/math-academy-id "q-120147" :question/problem "![](images/d2/d27af23ca398eba62c2ab1fe2ee2cf9bfdf736c16fdd8408d2a13e0d34dae32c.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/ab/ab076b61b443e031455f07c1e976467cc3b74651bfb5fc2fb39f89a74e156681.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $y=0$ and $y=2.$ Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\n- Second, the lines $y=0$ and $y=2$ divide the plane into $3$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $3$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| Region | $y<0$ | $0<y<2$ | $y>2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↘$ | $↗$ | $↗$ |\n| Sign | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}={y}^{2}(2-y)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $y=0$ and $y=2,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| Region | $y<0$ | $0<y<2$ | $y>2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Slope | $↗$ | $↗$ | $↘$ |\n| Sign | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=y(y-2)^{2}$ gives the required behavior.\n\n- The equation ${y}^{′}=y(y+2)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side evaluates to zero at $y=-2$ and $y=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=y(y-2)^{2}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172082 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd82d96b-34d5-5d20-b810-7ea88b0b5797" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Stationary Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db882f9a-0289-5f76-9569-86f733e96ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461929} {:answer/id #uuid "1df5b9ec-15de-54d9-9912-26f30bd3a4ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db882f9a-0289-5f76-9569-86f733e96ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461929} :answer-field/id #uuid "d28af0e5-6fb2-5c2d-9e5e-8126489054fe" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=x(3-y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462718} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d14b22ce-28bb-5e2e-97d1-bb0acb51ae7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461931} {:answer/id #uuid "fd484522-0fa7-5eeb-a1d2-a5ceba15bb76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d14b22ce-28bb-5e2e-97d1-bb0acb51ae7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461931} :answer-field/id #uuid "e50ca1e1-0158-5571-bc03-0ad8b185656a" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=(x+3)y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462719} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d2f3204-0315-5770-875c-0e96ce0575b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461933} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe5042f-ef3f-5b87-9a61-717250f8d8df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbe5042f-ef3f-5b87-9a61-717250f8d8df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461934} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dcc33f9-b8dc-57d3-928e-735493c6b377" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=(3-x)y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462720}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f78fc747-0bca-532e-9197-bd4cfa23233a" :question/math-academy-id "q-120228" :question/problem "![](images/20/204be6af825ef678e06526bff1fdac14ca5f09a2a7bee939620f3f2be1496985.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/90/9051213882bcb506ddae46e0a6a79c8cd03a10eadd89e0007f895f68b00c33de.png)\n\nNotice that the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=3$ and $y=0,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on these lines. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each equation:\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=x(3-y)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=x(3-y)$ evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $y=3.$\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=(x+3)y$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=(x+3)y$ evaluates to zero at $x=-3$ and $y=0.$\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=(3-x)y$ gives the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=(3-x)y$ evaluates to zero at $x=3$ and $y=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=(3-x)y$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253665 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172018 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "244419de-9b13-5923-b0a5-1bdc6f9b03b2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using the Sign of the Slopes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cabb5ac-1ea4-58ca-8ec2-a47cd57cff54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461935} {:answer/id #uuid "37d8eb56-6a47-5c3c-be71-00b9afff5a3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37d8eb56-6a47-5c3c-be71-00b9afff5a3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461936} :answer-field/id #uuid "2044208e-d2cd-5ef8-ac7c-3b2e9445c05e" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=x(3-y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462721} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d099f48-04e6-5ec3-9d4a-22f1add13d95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461937} {:answer/id #uuid "6f45a67b-6036-5ad5-acae-ada4d0516876" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d099f48-04e6-5ec3-9d4a-22f1add13d95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461937} :answer-field/id #uuid "da5b51e4-78c1-55c4-a59c-37bdc1fc7f96" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}={x}^{2}(y-3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462722} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c437f9b6-3688-50fc-bc30-6c81b716fd98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461939} {:answer/id #uuid "a1e6f80b-afce-50d2-960b-72e39d2880c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c437f9b6-3688-50fc-bc30-6c81b716fd98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461939} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f175659-1068-5c6b-90ee-cd9577815130" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=x(y-3)^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9d55cc1b-b5c1-5142-aa9a-80b5b9474cd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-120232" :question/problem "![](images/be/be758c93cb1e04380de9b57103c302623400342946996030b22ae12046488172.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/3a/3afe29e9dd507cd9aae4035ef3bde2f3f2c1865cd258c4d218ec1934d8626a6e.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=0$ and $y=3,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\n- Second, the lines $x=0$ and $y=3$ divide the plane into $4$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $4$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| $y>3$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<3$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=x(3-y)$ gives the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=x(3-y)$ evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $y=3,$ and the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| $y>3$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<3$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}(y-3)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}(y-3)$ evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $y=3,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| $y>3$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<3$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=x(y-3)^{2}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=x(y-3)^{2}$ evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $y=3,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| $y>3$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<3$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=x(3-y)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172018 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "244419de-9b13-5923-b0a5-1bdc6f9b03b2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using the Sign of the Slopes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bde1f724-b9ed-5e79-a94a-02a1a6dfc100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461941} {:answer/id #uuid "e23ece2c-ad5c-5961-89b9-83eae7e540a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bde1f724-b9ed-5e79-a94a-02a1a6dfc100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461941} :answer-field/id #uuid "07727b91-2a74-5a11-9b3c-826cbee53821" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=x(y-2)^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462724} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8deac526-bb02-5e05-8d47-64b0a595f894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461943} {:answer/id #uuid "753c6493-fd12-5a3d-8388-f609ae62f72a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8deac526-bb02-5e05-8d47-64b0a595f894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461943} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba1d1cdd-f545-52b2-b8f5-761b466c19b0" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=(x-2)^{2}y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462725} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3df85f6e-d3a8-5e14-87ac-d7f961d6161e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461945} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d477ea-75dd-57bf-9ac6-e6f6978946fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6d477ea-75dd-57bf-9ac6-e6f6978946fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461946} :answer-field/id #uuid "170738a9-c9c5-5683-8e04-01f73ca38ca6" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=(x-2)y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e5c81757-4f06-5306-9513-674ada3bee66" :question/math-academy-id "q-120235" :question/problem "![](images/19/19f3d391ff30338ae70f59f1cf1ad40922eb8146c2be0993253a99173db2925a.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/e3/e337a67c316dbee9e9c73849f363a7b2c3e3cb485bfef8eb49e87c3e33b98cf1.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=2$ and $y=0,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\n- Second, the lines $x=2$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into $4$ regions. The sign of the slopes in each of the $4$ regions are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| $y>0$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ |\n|  | $x<2$ | $x>2$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=x(y-2)^{2}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=x(y-2)^{2}$ evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $y=2.$\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=(x-2)^{2}y$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=(x-2)^{2}y$ evaluates to zero at $x=2$ and $y=0,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| $y>0$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<2$ | $x>2$ |\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=(x-2)y$ gives the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=(x-2)y$ evaluates to zero at $x=2$ and $y=0,$ and the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| $y>0$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<2$ | $x>2$ |\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=(x-2)y$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172017 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1616167b-5679-5ff6-b385-3e1b59352c64" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using the Sign of the Slopes and Factoring"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "255bfb79-2cba-5465-937b-caf746105f5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461947} {:answer/id #uuid "aff87299-0c98-5402-89b8-1c98dde911b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "255bfb79-2cba-5465-937b-caf746105f5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461947} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9aa1f4e-b107-5c2c-b70e-d39d16494d1b" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=4-y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462727} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56eeb9bf-b105-5e60-bb30-0b9e8040a113" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461949} {:answer/id #uuid "d2026974-2425-57a0-b5f3-22067869706c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2026974-2425-57a0-b5f3-22067869706c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461950} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b187ec4-67ae-58db-9366-bfea4458b68e" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=8y-2xy$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462728} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "835d86f0-81e9-5b09-b573-11ea9fc2288e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461951} {:answer/id #uuid "9bdae115-24b0-5254-9d73-9f5fe83ef6e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "835d86f0-81e9-5b09-b573-11ea9fc2288e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461951} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dd63a89-fab3-5f78-aa41-d933136e45b2" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}={x}^{2}y-8xy+16y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b482f1cd-a6f6-5695-b088-921969df414d" :question/math-academy-id "q-120264" :question/problem "![](images/f4/f4a6aa53604ce4381a6627097ba4ebc5853a67ff9fa1675b98e5114775cefdc6.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/7d/7d0d7ff6fa9c7cd074fcc2321f125ac5da8142e55578459f44903555e2797204.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=4$ and $y=0,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\n- Second, the lines $x=4$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into $4$ quarters. The sign of the slopes in each of the $4$ quarters are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| $y>0$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ |\n|  | $x<4$ | $x>4$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=4-y$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4-y\n$$\n\nevaluates to zero at $y=4$ only.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=8y-2xy$ gives the required behavior. The right-hand side of\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=8y-2xy=2y(4-x)\n$$\n\nevaluates to zero at $x=4$ and $y=0,$ and the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| $y>0$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n|  | $x<4$ | $x>4$ |\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}y-8xy+16y$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}y-8xy+16y=(x-4)^{2}y\n$$\n\nevaluates to zero at $x=4$ and $y=0,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| $y>0$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<4$ | $x>4$ |\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=8y-2xy$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256374 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172017 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1616167b-5679-5ff6-b385-3e1b59352c64" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using the Sign of the Slopes and Factoring"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fee2dfd7-aacc-5bab-b380-80ce1b3c6e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461953} {:answer/id #uuid "7ceb8d60-769b-56d1-a052-ca2e518a8519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fee2dfd7-aacc-5bab-b380-80ce1b3c6e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461953} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3f70fd4-c004-574a-b99c-c5e832b510e3" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=2y-xy$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462730} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c071070-22dc-55b5-8832-791294130da0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461955} {:answer/id #uuid "50718f8a-88b0-5fe8-8378-6ebcf7955fb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c071070-22dc-55b5-8832-791294130da0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461955} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9ba8bb8-3e0a-51fe-a155-8db1f5712c70" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+4x{y}^{2}+4{y}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462731} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "632a3b3b-8e1c-5ecc-8b99-29c06ef9182b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461957} {:answer/id #uuid "230c455c-c7c6-5692-869d-456a00266cad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "230c455c-c7c6-5692-869d-456a00266cad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461958} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d50254a-3624-586a-8373-63455d5964ee" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=x{y}^{2}-2{y}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462732}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c9d7302-1f93-5f85-9a08-01c47b45f471" :question/math-academy-id "q-120266" :question/problem "![](images/26/26a0a41cc50b6d5cb586c52e6a4e6bd5bd324f3e13ad7eef4ee0d9eed18340ea.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/24/249aba327a8103645963ce95e7935019a279b4cf0d9306111c41172ae22f792b.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=2$ and $y=0,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\n- Second, the lines $x=2$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into $4$ quarters. The sign of the slopes in each of the $4$ quarters are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| $y>0$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ |\n|  | $x<2$ | $x>2$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=2y-xy$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2y-xy=(2-x)y\n$$\n\nevaluates to zero at $x=2$ and $y=0,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| $y>0$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n|  | $x<2$ | $x>2$ |\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+4x{y}^{2}+4{y}^{2}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+4x{y}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=(x+2)^{2}{y}^{2}\n$$\n\nevaluates to zero at $x=-2$ and $y=0.$\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=x{y}^{2}-2{y}^{2}$ gives the required behavior. The right-hand side of\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x{y}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=(x-2){y}^{2}\n$$\n\nevaluates to zero at $x=2$ and $y=0,$ and the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| $y>0$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n|  | $x<2$ | $x>2$ |\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=x{y}^{2}-2{y}^{2}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256376 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172017 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1616167b-5679-5ff6-b385-3e1b59352c64" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using the Sign of the Slopes and Factoring"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fe7f321-122a-5908-bfec-692b0ccf9a25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461959} {:answer/id #uuid "bbb67729-9cf4-59ba-ac49-d4a48a15e6d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fe7f321-122a-5908-bfec-692b0ccf9a25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461959} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6859827-04e2-5784-b1c8-d019fb7d7dfd" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=(x-1){y}^{2}-x+1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462733} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d6a42f1-881a-5ef0-a490-c7001db30f56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461961} {:answer/id #uuid "8ae44472-7252-5de4-b1a2-7a7952b9fd7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ae44472-7252-5de4-b1a2-7a7952b9fd7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461962} :answer-field/id #uuid "106320a4-ad45-57bc-8904-e80e77d21fe2" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=xy-y-(x-1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462734} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d556edc4-a8bd-511e-9220-bffe25e0de8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461963} {:answer/id #uuid "97ebdb27-70e5-5a27-bc8a-6948d329bb1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d556edc4-a8bd-511e-9220-bffe25e0de8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461963} :answer-field/id #uuid "e74edcde-9130-516d-960c-bb1e2a1e6960" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=y-1-x(y-1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "01d08d57-0bae-5647-8907-efecd1b71deb" :question/math-academy-id "q-120271" :question/problem "![](images/85/85fcea0ad26f7da26189c7611a851bfe228d3ad5d428dcba6c8299c8304540d1.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/dc/dc75845932358d060d5878a30f00fa01e2b7b54408bca308110a53ea654ae18c.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=1$ and $y=1,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\n- Second, the lines $x=1$ and $y=1$ divide the plane into $4$ quarters. The sign of the slopes in each of the $4$ quarters are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| $y>1$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<1$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ |\n|  | $x<1$ | $x>1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=(x-1){y}^{2}-x+1$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=(x-1){y}^{2}-x+1=(x-1)(y+1)(y-1)\n$$\n\nevaluates to zero at $x=1$ and $y=\\pm 1.$\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=xy-y-(x-1)$ gives the required behavior. The right-hand side of\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=xy-y-(x-1)=(x-1)(y-1)\n$$\n\nevaluates to zero at $x=1$ and $y=1,$ and the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| $y>1$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<1$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<1$ | $x>1$ |\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=y-1-x(y-1)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y-1-x(y-1)=(1-x)(y-1)\n$$\n\nevaluates to zero at $x=1$ and $y=1,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| $y>1$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<1$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n|  | $x<1$ | $x>1$ |\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=xy-y-(x-1)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256380 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172016 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3e3fdc8-67d0-5b46-9c6b-c1ec8d4ea24f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Asymptotes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb529d81-61f3-5c3a-9ee9-1db6044fbb28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461965} {:answer/id #uuid "7d60155f-814b-5688-b80c-ff69952ec3fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb529d81-61f3-5c3a-9ee9-1db6044fbb28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461965} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4d0f6ff-d5d7-5577-b526-af22d3855f19" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=-x{y}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462736} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6edd1c4-8271-5dbf-a1a6-4d911168312f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461967} {:answer/id #uuid "b0d84be9-03de-5a03-987f-f1a67f85e17f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6edd1c4-8271-5dbf-a1a6-4d911168312f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461967} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a3087f9-0cbe-58bf-bce0-511b72140cf0" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=-\\frac{y}{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462737} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1637f773-701a-5c85-a0b6-4ffc31761b76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461969} {:answer/id #uuid "490949a0-6a54-5bc2-b39c-42807015af84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "490949a0-6a54-5bc2-b39c-42807015af84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461970} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9d67781-1cc9-577e-b688-09b5d2ad50e6" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69c58940-535c-5bff-aff2-b382e99c5568" :question/math-academy-id "q-120282" :question/problem "![](images/e9/e90d9a160db2c75091253eaa8a8c815e92c45f988841683f5a4d18ca6a6ea7db.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/54/54932bcffbbe793d6e1f730e65570b19cfc3603ddb62eaf0a63ef2e5b0705979.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- For $y\\ne 0,$ the slopes of the slope field become horizontal at $x=0$ only.\n\n- For $x\\ne 0,$ the slopes of the slope field become vertical as $y\\to 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=-x{y}^{2}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=-x{y}^{2}$ evaluates to zero both on $x=0$ and $y=0.$\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{y}{x}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{y}{x}$ does not evaluate to zero on $x=0.$\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y}$ gives the required behavior. For $y\\ne 0,$ the right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y}$ evaluates to zero on $x=0$ only, and for $x\\ne 0,$ we have \n\n$$\n|{y}^{′}|=|\\frac{x}{y}|\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,y\\to 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256382 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172016 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3e3fdc8-67d0-5b46-9c6b-c1ec8d4ea24f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Asymptotes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24028a5c-fc2a-5757-95c5-78df4d0cc179" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461971} {:answer/id #uuid "760c4264-0da7-5eb1-8a0b-8412347f72fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "760c4264-0da7-5eb1-8a0b-8412347f72fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461972} :answer-field/id #uuid "e34f929c-d868-505a-bb9a-733002a961a3" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462739} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f217bb0-bbd9-5d04-a30d-6c5e3dfcf81c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461973} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ad550c-1c2e-5f14-b7d6-adc3613f08b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f217bb0-bbd9-5d04-a30d-6c5e3dfcf81c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461973} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8047f7e-d8cd-5916-af01-982dac9a2d4d" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462740} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffb959b7-7fe4-5f69-9d00-17a70a3a040e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461975} {:answer/id #uuid "4e86a2f3-3aa4-5510-b84b-c8d507d24505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffb959b7-7fe4-5f69-9d00-17a70a3a040e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461975} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebd353f5-57ff-53ce-af4b-56b82be925ee" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=\\frac{y+1}{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462741}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a8520070-e078-5b91-88f5-b7a922021b9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-120286" :question/problem "![](images/e8/e8b573c6c2c59123de46346ccfc717fa89a98f7838e643a5e82972d753383588.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/2f/2f654bc96d27ac53dd501b10c5beb0d1c7d04ff4f643c5044692afac26ca2ba8.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- For $x\\ne 0,$ the slopes of the slope field become horizontal at $y=0$ only.\n\n- For $y\\ne 0,$ the slopes of the slope field become vertical as $x\\to 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}$ gives the required behavior. For $x\\ne 0,$ the right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}$ evaluates to zero on $y=0$ only, and for $y\\ne 0,$ we have \n\n$$\n|{y}^{′}|=|-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}|\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}$ does not evaluate to zero on $y=0.$\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y+1}{x}$ does *not* give the required behavior. For $x\\ne 0,$ the right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y+1}{x}$ does not evaluate to zero on $y=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256390 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087750 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Polygon Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25500724-aa98-596b-82b6-9b3ebb902bc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461977} {:answer/id #uuid "aaaa5c1c-3c0c-5c95-9205-edde43dea07d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25500724-aa98-596b-82b6-9b3ebb902bc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461977} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae2357e3-28f1-5577-96c4-de9b326f8797" :answer-field/key "The point $(5,-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462742} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f4b1d29-224e-5f44-9bc0-f82a70d85395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461979} {:answer/id #uuid "d97fe64a-5a3d-52e8-9098-ef380defe0f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d97fe64a-5a3d-52e8-9098-ef380defe0f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461980} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f163c2c-63d3-50f4-81b1-c6703cce844b" :answer-field/key "The point $(-2,-5)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462743} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5042122-91ac-59ec-99fa-55f3f474d65f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461981} {:answer/id #uuid "5481e08c-1692-504b-8483-ff67bfb122b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461982}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5481e08c-1692-504b-8483-ff67bfb122b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461982} :answer-field/id #uuid "380a7507-2a2d-57f1-b070-a2ec0c065fad" :answer-field/key "The point $(3,12)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462744}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7fe1aa4a-edf0-5fec-a75f-5eaee41d4322" :question/math-academy-id "q-12033" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-2,1),(3,3),$ and $(5,-2).$ Which of the following are coordinates of a vertex of ${S}^{′}$, the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 12 & 13\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-2,-5),(3,12),(5,13).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is “The point $(-2,-5)$”; “The point $(3,12)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256410 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115181 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9a3d8db-a6e0-5c96-9c75-415d4a75cf4d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With No Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0558a439-02ce-5375-b541-6307b46bd5d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461983} {:answer/id #uuid "9ac22dc7-1624-5e98-8996-ecf54a359749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ac22dc7-1624-5e98-8996-ecf54a359749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461984} :answer-field/id #uuid "f655b146-b636-5304-b3ee-f5861980d1be" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462745} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e441a873-6a92-5d9b-b43a-06d11df0757c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461985} {:answer/id #uuid "f0c7571a-802a-51ec-9f6b-6d2f9e7443ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0c7571a-802a-51ec-9f6b-6d2f9e7443ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461986} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab15405d-16ad-5554-8fc1-f76cfab87ae6" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{6}{7}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462746} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bc9cc66-69ce-59c4-ae9d-b84f8046a244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461987} {:answer/id #uuid "6b3e070c-85a1-5d06-819a-6ff5d984da87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b3e070c-85a1-5d06-819a-6ff5d984da87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461988} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2cb80f3-bd22-527d-8b69-d6cf9583f235" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "735542a6-3adb-5150-94ab-7fbabf60bc01" :question/math-academy-id "q-120476" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions for $0\\le x<2\\pi ?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the range of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, equations $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5}$, $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{6}{7}$, and $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{3}$ have no solutions."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115181 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9a3d8db-a6e0-5c96-9c75-415d4a75cf4d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With No Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "223c445b-9a70-5067-bb3a-73307392586c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461989} {:answer/id #uuid "4aec07be-41ae-55b0-ae3e-0a620cfecd23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "223c445b-9a70-5067-bb3a-73307392586c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461989} :answer-field/id #uuid "8587961d-9189-5272-9fc9-9e4b89fddda8" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=-\\frac{3}{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462748} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca101ee8-ad1e-51e8-bde7-4bb8dbac9feb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461991} {:answer/id #uuid "2d7ac247-efbf-