-63a5f0ec8f97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "602a7c8d-0df8-5802-a275-63a5f0ec8f97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437665} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8a0ad93-ccff-5c53-b92c-06f494f55cfe" :answer-field/key "$G(x,y,z)$ $=x(y+1)\\,i$ $+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(y-z)\\,j$ $+{z}^{3}\\,k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438861}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09fffcb2-a27e-5da4-b160-3d4f79d02cb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-122688" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $D(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point $(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}$ to a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $E(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $G(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,y-z\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\\,n\\in Z}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $D(x,y,z)$ $=5\\,i$ $+{z}^{2}\\,j$ $+(y+x)\\,k$; $G(x,y,z)$ $=x(y+1)\\,i$ $+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(y-z)\\,j$ $+{z}^{3}\\,k$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256696 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-poin