 **not** conservative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464687} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49cfedf6-d49a-5e91-871d-064fdfe04a90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463508} {:answer/id #uuid "7f50c179-bb2d-543d-9a0e-64366e74bf4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49cfedf6-d49a-5e91-871d-064fdfe04a90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463508} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f1ce503-c45e-5c4f-b66f-0b20a268d4b7" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464688} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6335fb4-b7d2-5e25-96b9-fb86f54e128a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463510} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e90ff6-6b3a-5487-ad34-341eace46494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6335fb4-b7d2-5e25-96b9-fb86f54e128a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463510} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c0adfec-2ceb-58ea-8799-9876dc31d423" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0$ for some closed paths $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09907334-a616-5854-99eb-0e8232bc08ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-125651" :question/problem "Consider the scalar field $f(x,y)=\\frac{{e}^{xy}}{{x}^{2}+1}$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$∇f$ is **not** conservative” is false. The vector field $∇f$ is conservative by definition.\n\n- Statement “${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise smooth path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is false. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\n- Statement “${∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0$ for some closed paths $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is false. The circulation $Γ=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1da220a9-2afc-5b63-a423-a4d2b3de9567" :knowledge-point/title "Circulation in Conservative Vector Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33eaf71d-bc62-5906-8af4-6d36cba0d63d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463512} {:answer/id #uuid "c4f06b8d-cb5a-5739-8391-b845b7c84396" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4f06b8d-cb5a-5739-8391-b845b7c84396" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463513} :answer-field/id #uuid "92d363ac-f7c1-59e9-88fa-ae19dd41eb83" :answer-field/key "$∇f$ is conservativ